CP 5.6 / finding F1 — Variant F: cross-context reproduction
============================================================
Harness: f1_variantF_crossctx.cpp   (Mistral-7B L0 q_proj [4096,4096], M=1)
Builds:  c2c5d313 = libcipher_rt.so.pre_cp5_3_step2   (F1-broken)
         dc804eb3 = libcipher_rt.so                    (CP 5.3 STEP 2 fix)
degenerate gate: nan|inf | cos<0.85 | rel>0.35   (correct = rel~0.140 cos~0.9905)

Variant F = the structural element A-E could not express: a real SECOND
CUDA context. Create an 8-SM green CUcontext via the library's own
cipher_rt_green_ctx_ensure(); switch the caller onto it via
cipher_rt_green_ctx_make_current(); run cipher_rt_marlin_engine_dispatch;
read output buffer C from the green context with NO cross-context sync.
Per iter: memset(C,0) on green ; dispatch ; cuMemcpyDtoH(C) on green.

----- engine = c2c5d313 -----
GREEN: green context bound to group 2 with 8 SMs
[green] ensure rc=0   make_current rc=0   caller 0x..af0 -> 0x..b90  (primary=0x..af0)
    iter 0    nan=0 inf=0 zeros=0    rel=0.1400 cos=0.9905   ok
    iter 1..99  nan=0 inf=0 zeros=4096 max_abs=2.8789 rel=1.0000 cos=0.0000  <<< DEGENERATE
    iter 0 first 10:  engine = 0.00000 (all zeros) | ref = -0.261, 0.172, 0.333, ...
    control (after primary-context drain): rel=0.1400 cos=0.9905  ok
    degenerate iters: 99 / 100
    RESULT: BROKE — cross-context race reproduced

----- engine = dc804eb3 -----
GREEN: green context bound to group 6 with 8 SMs
[green] ensure rc=0  sm_count=8   make_current rc=0   caller -> green
    iter 0    nan=0 inf=0 zeros=0    rel=0.1400 cos=0.9905   ok
    iter 99   nan=0 inf=0 zeros=0    rel=0.1400 cos=0.9905   ok
    iter 0 first 10:  engine = -0.286, 0.174, 0.325, ... | ref = -0.261, 0.172, ...
    control (after primary-context drain): rel=0.1400 cos=0.9905  ok
    degenerate iters: 0 / 100
    RESULT: PASS — output stayed correct

============================================================
VARIANT F VERDICT — F1 ROOT CAUSE CONFIRMED.

c2c5d313: 99/100 iterations degenerate. The degenerate output is exactly
the memset-0 prefill (zeros=4096) — the green-context cuMemcpyDtoH reads
buffer C *before* the primary-context GEMM has written it. The GEMM math
is sound: the post-loop control re-read, taken after explicitly draining
the PRIMARY context, returns the correct rel=0.140/cos=0.9905. The only
defect is the missing cross-context ordering.

  Mechanism: c2c5d313 cipher_rt_marlin_engine_dispatch wraps the GEMM
  launch UNCONDITIONALLY in PrimaryCtxGuard -> cuCtxSetCurrent(primary), so
  the GEMM and its write to C execute on the PRIMARY context's NULL stream.
  The caller (and the consuming read) are on the GREEN context. Two
  contexts, two independent NULL streams, no cross-context event/sync ->
  the consumer races the producer. In a real decode the consumer is the
  next decode kernel (attention / residual) reading the logits/activation
  buffer; it reads zeros/garbage -> NaN-free all-zero logits -> argmax(0)
  -> the `<unk>` token-0 repetition signature recorded in F1.

dc804eb3: 0/100. CP 5.3 STEP 2 scopes PrimaryCtxGuard out when a green
context is active (engine.cpp:1005 `if (green_ctx_sm_count()==0)`), so the
GEMM launches green-bound on the CALLER's context, grid sized to the 8-SM
partition (engine.cpp:812-813). Producer and consumer share the green NULL
stream -> ordered -> coherent. The STEP 2 green-context guard-scoping fixes
F1 as a side-effect.

Provenance (direct, not inferred): `nm -D` shows cipher_rt_green_ctx_sm_count
is EXPORTED in dc804eb3 but ABSENT from c2c5d313 — c2c5d313's dispatch
structurally cannot contain the green-skip branch. md5: c2c5d313 =
c2c5d313e2c24b687ba344cd9fe14a2f, dc804eb3 = dc804eb3b2796652342852f75763d5ed.

Both predicted outcomes met:
  (a) the bug is the cross-context race  — CONFIRMED
  (b) dc804eb3 fixes it via green-context guard scoping — CONFIRMED

NEXT: F1 root cause is established. The full-GPU path in any future build
must not pin the GEMM to a context different from the caller's without a
cross-context dependency (event wait). dc804eb3 already does this for the
green-active path; a fix STEP for the full-GPU build, plus the 3.617x tok/W
re-measurement with a correctness gate, is the remaining CP 5.6 scope.
